28021      title 'Gasoline and Emissions Data';
28022      data gas;
28023      set sashelp.gas;
28024      if fuel in ('Ethanol', '82rongas', 'Gasohol');
28025      run;

NOTE: There were 171 observations read from the data set SASHELP.GAS.
NOTE: The data set WORK.GAS has 112 observations and 4 variables.

28026      ods graphics on;
28027      * Request a Spline Transformation of Equivalence Ratio;
28028      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 plots=(transformation obp residuals);
28029      model identity(nox) = spline(EqRatio / nknots=4);
28030      run;

NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1727.

28031      * Separate Curves and Intercepts;
28032      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 additive plots=(transformation obp);
28033      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none) |
28034      spline(EqRatio / nknots=4 after);
28035      run;

NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1728.

28036      * Separate Intercepts;
28037      proc transreg data=Gas solve ss2 additive;
28038      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none)
28039      spline(EqRatio / nknots=4);
28040      run;

NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: There were 112 observations read from the data set WORK.GAS.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE TRANSREG printed page 1729.

28041      * Separate Curves and Intercepts with Penalized B-Splines;
28042      proc transreg data=Gas ss2 plots=transformation lprefix=0;
28043      model identity(nox) = class(Fuel / zero=none) * pbspline(EqRatio);
28044      run;

NOTE: AFTER is assumed when PBSPLINE is crossed with a CLASS variable.
NOTE: Since the model contains SMOOTH, BSPLINE, PBSPLINE, or a CLASS expansion with ZERO=NONE, a model with an implicit intercept is fit.
NOTE: All statistics are mean corrected.
NOTE: 2 observations were deleted from the analysis due to missing values.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
